0b43dcf97f56b0fd33517a09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98527" :question/id #uuid "796023e8-480d-5ead-996f-d9e2e236082e" :question/math-academy-id "q-98527" :question/problem "Which of the following is the phase line of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{2}-12y-35?$" :question/worked-solution "To draw the phase line of the differential equation, we proceed using the following three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find the equilibrium solutions of the differential equation. \n\nIn this case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}-12y-35 & =0 \\\\ -({y}^{2}+12y+35) & =0 \\\\ -(y+7)(y+5) & =0 \\\\ y & =-7,-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium solutions are $y=-7$ and $y=-5.$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the intervals of $y$ for which $f(y)>0$ and $f(y)<0.$ \n\nConstructing a sign table, we get the following:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-7)$ | $(-7,-5)$ | $(-5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-(y+7)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $y+5$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-7,-5),$ and negative for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-7)\\cup (-5,\\infty ).$\n\n**Step 3**: Draw the phase line using the following recipe:\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/b08c48590fe2538666e0e3a559c123b0f5cd3bb35680f2c98d3c14691780a575.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-98527/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66924d52-fd39-5308-b78e-611e3d3129ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98526/selection/