\n\n- $f(y)>0$ when $y\\in (2,\\infty ).$\n\n- $f(y)<0$ when $y\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,2).$\n\nTherefore, we can draw the phase line using the following recipe:\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/d970e9a23302139dfc40db62a8a2697f2a2d68b7523b40e0f8268b587eb904fb.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97918/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36070a0f-0b40-5fa6-9357-9f0c754b00a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97918"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336034/selection/0fc576b6bd8e64ba8cb952e1a42df5620a7be551f61e76d15d55919cbc3de79d" :answer/id #uuid "9052447a-5b9a-54b0-ae77-4d8bf171ab22" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/2a04842b64d6b282ec0856e9f4fd8d7a5654319a9af73ab217091cb3af95fc07.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336034/selection/5f1ffa02f1808ee34c382bc3b7204373195a649f13274173699cceb50ad6c8c2" :answer/id #uuid "422e6dae-495e-5601-91e9-f062d4acfc6e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/8d72bdb44dff1b7d97a256e411a6696e3cf372b313774356037da137d03318d2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336034/selection/cf2d4c59e12c0b546e937034060f205f155baa38e50b5c3d83b3f0a5899a8ea1" :answer/id #uuid "f64272b9-7840-554f-9a42-b03cdddfab75" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/aa22eb5ee0909281679861d59a269f079e8b596790390d036e53b65010dc70d8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336034/selection/91c3493e0bff89ed07ed1f849591009f872d299a989d4f1826dd73b4831b241a" :answer/id #uuid "6ce4f56b-d329-5b97-8654-7d148eaa62fb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/1b10afb2caebfdd7d804f96b4bea7c7ae5e77ac8c381b5ce88e9b4c4b776bd47.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336034/selection/2f5cf4a1956f911e611048548c9199b67ec10ba4e5c02430f90b1ef28117b5c1" :answer/id #uuid "9cc66e8c-8581-5394-ab55-2d69d4b59f7b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/aff15abfa4145efb37ed319424f89097a333fce28e7ca4d91713283a360f280b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336034/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a76267a-a6c0-5831-8601-82ec8b1d502d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-336034/selection/91c3493e0bff89ed07ed1f849591009f872d299a989d4f1826dd73b4831b241a" :answer-field/choices ["q-336034/selection/0fc576b6bd8e64ba8cb952e1a42df5620a7be551f61e76d15d55919cbc3de79d" "q-336034/selection/5f1ffa02f1808ee34c382bc3b7204373195a649f13274173699cceb50ad6c8c2" "q-336034/selection/cf2d4c59e12c0b546e937034060f205f155baa38e50b5c3d83b3f0a5899a8ea1" "q-336034/selection/91c3493e0bff89ed07ed1f849591009f872d299a989d4f1826dd73b4831b241a" "q-336034/selection/2f5cf4a1956f911e611048548c9199b67ec10ba4e5c02430f90b1ef28117b5c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336034" :question/id #uuid "0a5df75f-ce9d-5773-a201-b1413c58dd16" :question/math-academy-id "q-336034" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/e6a178edcc79e9e36553acf436209525b490dbefde06823d571f8e317dab0086.png)\n\nThe slope field of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx}=f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following is the phase line of the given equation?" :question/worked-solution "From the slope field, we can deduce the following:\n\n- $y=-1$ and $y=1$ are equilibrium solutions.\n\n- For all $y\\in (1,\\infty ),$ the slopes of the slope field are positive. Therefore, $f(y)>0$ in this region.\n\n- For all $y\\in (-1,1),$ the slopes of the slope field are negative. Therefore, $f(y)<0$ in this region.\n\n- For all $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1),$ the slopes of the slope field are negative. Therefore, $f(y)<0$ in this region.\n\nNow, we can draw the phase line using the following recipe:\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis.\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions.\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0.$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0.$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/62b3d23025e8b2716dd584678f1aef2ba3132a66250d0999cb13a2281347ee89.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336034/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c72cc6e0-deae-51fc-a5e4-b27fcb6f7892"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-96515"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/cbccf40aca753c4c23cc2b159697deca70b45844d2cbf458c9a04f6dc6d3026f.png)\n\nThe phase line of a differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be the slope field of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "From the phase line, we can deduce the following:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-2$ and $y=0.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along these lines.\n\n- $f(y)<0$ for $y<-2.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are negative in this region.\n\n- $f(y)>0$ for $-2<y<0$ or $y>0.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are positive in these regions.\n\nThe only slope field that satisfies the above conditions is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/64d0e59ba56d8c2a582cc80d267c258681f26badf2b77fddb79c3ff17bdd7249.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-98044/selection/2439e3455da2ff112c365a375d4f570b566bc030d6fc11ac4270008347bc2d46" :answer/id #uuid "984fb1e9-ae3f-5c2e-9d49-ae767fbf14c5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/4497b384ad4d9dd3812b6953cc691f5a8f7c3b8e0b8e1d88095af0d9cbefcf96.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98044/selection/6185b50bcef5492cf9d9fe5b678032ebe3cf72f18af98f43c4d74e736f31f83e" :answer/id #uuid "a909c6d5-0b94-53ae-aa6f-aebd056afbf2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/44419413221f356bac454f1aa070e3888a8ea6921db3f7c69033e7b4347f46ec.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98044/selection/0124c87d8bcbee9cd80964aa92ecac908805aee0145c6a50fff26ed112beee86" :answer/id #uuid "dda18b9f-d1e8-5659-9f3f-f0ad044c9adf" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/8abe546b96547089599251ce0c45db7e64afe957a50d18ec5d4e734c15cb7954.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98044/selection/b56b1f297a56fe748fb1fbe633bebb6bdcdb4e076d97ee60b5940dffb31e59b8" :answer