ine, we can deduce the following:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-2$ and $y=0.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along these lines.\n\n- $f(y)<0$ for $y\\in (-2,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are negative in these regions.\n\n- $f(y)>0$ for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-2).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are positive in this region.\n\nThe only slope field that satisfies the above conditions is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/44419413221f356bac454f1aa070e3888a8ea6921db3f7c69033e7b4347f46ec.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98044/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c72cc6e0-deae-51fc-a5e4-b27fcb6f7892"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98044"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98042/selection/ae597ff59675357bdd899eed51af157f3e75b1a84914f740c89efed24b563c9a" :answer/id #uuid "bddbfadf-045b-552e-94e9-718194bfdd24" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/40f87baa0460a6efb4e1f1c994edda1b28ddc6e7cfc070535101a7b4b15d7075.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98042/selection/327efb36c736478984766f051a5d9780e6eab53d71072626d49ec84f50eb6842" :answer/id #uuid "20cdc014-32f6-52b7-80e2-eefa89c778e3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/9a392f874252df611fc92421b98d19f930ac6efe7bd43e82ef2b286cda2b70bc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98042/selection/31c3438a53c5e22b1ea6c86cda9c59e78440d4888b263bbda398ae1af6d03aef" :answer/id #uuid "19a1d83a-852f-57ab-8d51-8c5cd24a9e80" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/