4aac304110ed4743b58ba786141cecc404791130bf35884f8fbefe94c18fbd6.png)\n\nThe phase line of a differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be the slope field of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "From the phase line, we can deduce the following:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-2$ and $y=2.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along these lines.\n\n- $f(y)<0$ for $y\\in (-2,2).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are negative in this region.\n\n- $f(y)>0$ for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are positive in these regions.\n\nThe only slope field that satisfies the above conditions is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/eb76b700066be49d493fe0738b7c3b18b0b34dcaada93f7c961e5647a0a079c1.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98042/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c72cc6e0-deae-51fc-a5e4-b27fcb6f7892"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98038/selection/29aaaf58e46fb856396f574c79562700c1b1e7070956e37c744520a12a4a07cf" :answer/id #uuid "3ae9b70e-87af-5e1c-bda3-797eb6fbb20d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/bbb6defd12fdc683f2df111cce7e10807fd8d69877ddf12de7fa97d3e9d53781.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98038/selection/73a2490eb53b5a3e653251075ff6537489165175ca26d9f41e5fa1cb8c5544c0" :answer/id #uuid "cc9a5c4b-8eeb-59ee-a97b-ae9c87a10964" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/d281794a12395bdbe1a39d23403b59c0d1638820e9951628cf11cedb